acher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1"}],"sha":"df26a4b23ee599d9f7a80b2d27053eea9c21c91a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/df26a4b23ee599d9f7a80b2d27053eea9c21c91a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7741667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kmye","id":7741667,"login":"kmye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDE2Njc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:21:36Z","email":"eileen_kang@tech.gov.sg","name":"Eileen Kang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:21:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add custom student groups feature module (#6) (#59)\n\nMigrate the Custom Student Groups platform capability from the legacy PG\ncodebase. This adds a complete /groups feature with CRUD operations,\nExcel upload, staff sharing, and multi-select delete — covering all six\nsub-issues (#27–#32).\n\n\n\nfix: preserve group name when navigating to add-students\n\nThe group name was lost on return from add-students because the\nCreateGroupPage re-initialized with an empty name. Now groupName is\npassed through navigation state in both directions.\n\n\n\nfix: make student table rows clickable to toggle selection\n\nClicking anywhere on a row now toggles that student''s checkbox.\nstopPropagation on the checkbox cell prevents a double-toggle.\n\n\n\nfix: align custom groups mock data with raw PGW wire format\n\nThe fetchCustomGroups mapper expects the raw PGW shape (id, groupName,\nowners[], studentsList[]) but the fixture used the already-mapped shape\n(customGroupId, name, studentCount). This caused group names and student\ncounts to render as undefined/0.\n\n\n\nfeat: make assigned group cards clickable with class detail page\n\nAssigned class cards now link to /groups/classes/:classId which shows\nthe class name, level, year, and student roster. CCA groups remain\nstatic as there is no CCA detail endpoint.\n\n\n\nfeat: add CCA group detail page and make CCA cards clickable\n\nCCA cards in the assigned groups section now link to\n/groups/ccas/:ccaId which shows the CCA name and student roster.\n\n\n\nfix: change CCA detail route to /groups/cca/details/:ccaId\n\nThe previous /groups/ccas/:id path was invented — it doesn''t exist in\nthe source PG codebase. Updated to /groups/cca/details/:id per project\nconvention.\n\n\n\nfix: align detail mock student count with list fixture (12 students)\n\nThe list endpoint showed 12 students but the detail endpoint only\nreturned 5, causing a mismatch between the table card and the detail\npage.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4eb1e52350bfae77d4262a0f4daf7a93ef356c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/git/trees/4eb1e52350bfae77d4262a0f4daf7a93ef356c13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/git/commits/e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1","verification":{"payload":"tree 4eb1e52350bfae77d4262a0f4daf7a93ef356c13\nparent f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0\nauthor Eileen Kang <eileen_kang@tech.gov.sg> 1781270496 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781270496 +0000\n\nfeat: add custom student groups feature module (#6) (#59)\n\nMigrate the Custom Student Groups platform capability from the legacy PG\ncodebase. This adds a complete /groups feature with CRUD operations,\nExcel upload, staff sharing, and multi-select delete — covering all six\nsub-issues (#27–#32).\n\n\n\nfix: preserve group name when navigating to add-students\n\nThe group name was lost on return from add-students because the\nCreateGroupPage re-initialized with an empty name. Now groupName is\npassed through navigation state in both directions.\n\n\n\nfix: make student table rows clickable to toggle selection\n\nClicking anywhere on a row now toggles that student''s checkbox.\nstopPropagation on the checkbox cell prevents a double-toggle.\n\n\n\nfix: align custom groups mock data with raw PGW wire format\n\nThe fetchCustomGroups mapper expects the raw PGW shape (id, groupName,\nowners[], studentsList[]) but the fixture used the already-mapped shape\n(customGroupId, name, studentCount). This caused group names and student\ncounts to render as undefined/0.\n\n\n\nfeat: make assigned group cards clickable with class detail page\n\nAssigned class cards now link to /groups/classes/:classId which shows\nthe class name, level, year, and student roster. CCA groups remain\nstatic as there is no CCA detail endpoint.\n\n\n\nfeat: add CCA group detail page and make CCA cards clickable\n\nCCA cards in the assigned groups section now link to\n/groups/ccas/:ccaId which shows the CCA name and student roster.\n\n\n\nfix: change CCA detail route to /groups/cca/details/:ccaId\n\nThe previous /groups/ccas/:id path was invented — it doesn''t exist in\nthe source PG codebase. Updated to /groups/cca/details/:id per project\nconvention.\n\n\n\nfix: align detail mock student count with list fixture (12 students)\n\nThe list endpoint showed 12 students but the detail endpoint only\nreturned 5, causing a mismatch between the table card and the detail\npage.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLAfxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvDQQAGbgc6mvnET/ABKGSdmhW2Yv\nFgzEpnNz0TDey7aLoR5IobEh4r14N7KTR205sS+2w0ayoNM1WlkGYoTyYo3ExjnL\ni/3qRnM8oP4whdOxAEj9lwGHQV+FxhJ3QOEB9dcKZc8dXiLefl26KSfOIvrcTpht\nmvxJmmqizdpj+hYCNVQqP6v5HSJM5GJKqmmWeEvQp0C+V6Ck97jphxtxIfMoG11m\ndGT248uL468bb9HluBLzwliFJT/U+MNZVWofJVRU1+iGauKXj/GJ1QaoQfnq7EP3\nfkfVXzf+7pVQ+LPX9DI6lSKhIowr5SJnD5hdJMrqAeCJieRqsbrn/8WmK9xMM28n\nMKzf5Dbn3jFQJ79I/WCbyBeqVFPvMNcPjQrjrU5qIDjgRj47kZX/086A37DFTSxs\nIeFk66ZSN5D7cMksgU3VyFDNZK4YO/yay2DVXvGDJpclFbHRgpm/5dzzxmB2BvQW\n6/TQaA3vlmiDxilcCAxFjZao1JmW03HAjyBJgMKynZbe2IDoAtDJBjm55RS0pqlR\nQn00sANr3GjURHkgl5WjiEUG9Y4ZBth5KuPEfMRkLwQCK/XPRhvbyK8cHpLzaMuk\nBVrb/XT8mAj3FY9mupfre9Zn7yLjyETBMC1yXRhfV8dVPdV0PDyzJvoVttgZmcxn\nEnhwvepaPBlrB4Z3CYVo\n=5DSW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T13:21:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commit/e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1","node_id":"C_kwDOTSo9BNoAKGU1MDQzZmYwZTdkYTE3ZDA1MDc4NmNjYTQyZjEwMTM5OTQ5YWQzYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commit/f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0","sha":"f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0"}],"sha":"e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/e5043ff0e7da17d050786cca42f10139949ad3b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7741667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kmye","id":7741667,"login":"kmye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDE2Njc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmye","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/commits/f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T11:57:01Z","email":"eileen_kang@tech.gov.sg","name":"Eileen Kang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T11:57:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: add MAX_QUESTIONS guard to reducer and improve ReminderSection UX (#5) (#58)\n\n- Add MAX_QUESTIONS (5) boundary check in ADD_QUESTION reducer action\n  to prevent state bypass when UI button is disabled\n- Disable ReminderSection when no due date is set (wrap in fieldset,\n  show \"Set a due date first\" helper text)\n- Add comprehensive reducer tests for consent form actions:\n  SET_DUE_DATE, SET_REMINDER, SET_RESPONSE_TYPE, question CRUD,\n  SET_EVENT, SET_VENUE (21 new test cases)\n- Add validation edge case tests for reminder date window,\n  past due dates, and upload-in-flight blocking (13 new test cases)\n- Add QuestionBuilder component tests (14 test cases)\n- Add ReminderSection component tests (14 test cases)\n\n\n\nfix: use native radio inputs in ReminderSection and Calendar in DueDateSection (#5)\n\n- Replace RadioGroup/RadioGroupItem with native radio inputs in\n  ReminderSection — the RadioGroup component''s Children.map only\n  passes controlled props to direct children, but the radio inputs\n  were nested inside <label> elements and never received them.\n- Switch DueDateSection from native <input type=\"date\"> to the\n  Calendar component (same pattern as EventScheduleSection).\n- Use early return for disabled state instead of <fieldset disabled>\n  to avoid interaction issues with nested form controls.\n\n\n\nfix: replace native date input with Calendar popover in ReminderSection (#5)\n\nReplace the reminder date <input type=\"date\"> with the same Calendar +\nPopover pattern used by DueDateSection and EventScheduleSection for\nconsistent date picker UX across the form.\n\n\n\nfix: add month/year navigation to Calendar component (#5)\n\nThe Calendar stub only showed the current month with no way to\nnavigate. Add prev/next month buttons and display the month/year\nheader so users can pick dates in any month.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91694c452baa5d0af72285edad0e359957bd3c4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/git/trees/91694c452baa5d0af72285edad0e359957bd3c4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gracestl/teacher-workspace-pg-frontend/git/commits/f7c7f96259c7281841f0afd7e7e0bd37751322d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 91694c452baa5d0af72285edad0e359957bd3c4f\nparent cf2951191453490674594bfb97c9986ba3b0d3d7\nauthor Eileen Kang <eileen_kang@tech.gov.sg> 1781265421 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781265421 +0000\n\nfix: add MAX_QUESTIONS guard to reducer and improve ReminderSection UX (#5) (#58)\n\n- Add MAX_QUESTIONS (5) boundary check in ADD_QUESTION reducer action\n  to prevent state bypass when UI button is disabled\n- Disable ReminderSection when no due date is set (wrap in fieldset,\n  show \"Set a due date first\" helper text)\n- Add comprehensive reducer tests for consent form actions:\n  SET_DUE_DATE, SET_REMINDER, SET_RESPONSE_TYPE, question CRUD,\n  SET_EVENT, SET_VENUE (21 new test cases)\n- Add validation edge case tests for reminder date window,\n  past due dates, and upload-in-flight blocking (13 new test cases)\n- Add QuestionBuilder component tests (14 test cases)\n- Add ReminderSection component tests (14 test cases)\n\n\n\nfix: use native radio inputs in ReminderSection and Calendar in DueDateSection (#5)\n\n- Replace RadioGroup/RadioGroupItem with native radio inputs in\n  ReminderSection — the RadioGroup component''s Children.map only\n  passes controlled props to direct children, but the radio inputs\n  were nested inside <label> elements and never received them.\n- Switch DueDateSection from native <input type=\"date\"> to the\n  Calendar component (same pattern as EventScheduleSection).\n- Use early return for disabled state instead of <fieldset disabled>\n  to avoid interaction issues with nested form controls.\n\n\n\nfix: replace native date input with Calendar popover in ReminderSection (#5)\n\nReplace the reminder date <input type=\"date\"> with the same Calendar +\nPopover pattern used by DueDateSection and EventScheduleSection for\nconsistent date picker UX across the form.\n\n\n\nfix: add month/year navigation to Calendar component (#5)\n\nThe Calendar stub only showed the current month with no way to\nnavigate. Add prev/next month buttons and display the month/year\nheader so users can pick dates in any month.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK/QdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmswQAG0dCTHoCG800RkKA7f1gB3B\nx6RsyPc19QP6f6c0frrUhl5rfvNnpuUv+NsWYGzCegHLbVq3YZ0Lqp8Zp8FCLfN1\nt7NNSeYl7nBuGnprfGY64SoZmh0dXznuZn7g95Fseh/N3iDwAprJdQVHJtNezI+a\nkPNVHZgY1N4gQgsWM8Vmg4/P7U28FSv6JUk/qrhz3RiO07FIgguwRy4Fg6OAkmmN\neKItstE/6cPetBuq9C7Bz3bDjkib9bFj6EelHVSbk+EYtnc6+E+caUB6ycww0vEs\n1rh9lQUbEcBo5IAmvbaziGdokh4ewl0TwJTjn5YErMi0cv99cuixblDOIoitRQiR\nGhA7Wo8j1aRNaDzRPFi8+es4luXIk7w1v1aREmLQF3NVgbpel4mM+LnK0wDTMEH/\n88TB0t9yxqxJdpT2yJ1yfVN1YektR/ymadiVu139vf4jDdEqO+YJIG5rvvce561M\nYHHDFwADJGlXuWHr/dWdt5rr9nZhYeZsT4raifknoKyC5NPuoM76qK6u2EFhDIg7\nib+wehAoAEJ0/vfxtwOIkAazzCi6O4eeyPjvliV37Pp110tt9xBGTPGpc2LYhZRr\nkWj27IL/4uNfpXXaJH3VfKTg6l0+pnRHjj+KFpODwvP0RmemiCoFGhr7uO/rS3FC\ng//U0Xu45cRzLcTvcxdh\n=hz3D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T11:57:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_u