"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/openmini/commits/9af840011794c2d332d514f9d823c203645dd62c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T12:09:47Z","email":"brahimvall.boumouzouna@etu.fstm.ac.ma","name":"Brahim Vall Boumouzouna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T12:11:22Z","email":"92952971+BoumouzounaBrahimVall@users.noreply.github.com","name":"BOUMOUZOUNA BRAHIM VALL"},"message":"docs(security): add OTA updates and app store policy section\n\nStates plainly that mini-apps fall under the WebView exemption in both\nstores'' policies (Apple 2.5.2, Google Play device-and-network-abuse),\nthat this is not a review bypass for substantial feature changes, and\nthat policy compliance is the integrator''s obligation. Points to the\nimmutable-version registry design as the machinery for gating and\nrolling back mini-app releases like any production deploy.\n\nPrompted by launch-thread feedback.","tree":{"sha":"16e153f48d70bb760ea3e9bc27e698e2a3965840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/openmini/git/trees/16e153f48d70bb760ea3e9bc27e698e2a3965840"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/openmini/git/commits/9af840011794c2d332d514f9d823c203645dd62c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92952971?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BoumouzounaBrahimVall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Boumouzoun