author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commits/f4450de0c12b3f78eccb04161576b7c8f79cc1bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:16:53Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:16:53Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"fix(booking): check availability in Step 1 so users can''t pick booked rooms\n\nPreviously the booking flow fetched ALL rooms in Step 1 (via /api/rooms)\nand let users select any of them — including rooms already booked for\ntheir chosen dates. The availability check only ran at the final submit\n(POST /api/reservations), so users filled in all their guest details\nand got ''Room is not available for the selected dates'' at the very end.\n\nFix:\n- Step1Dates now queries /api/rooms/availability when dates are valid\n  and marks already-booked rooms with a ''Booked'' badge + greyscale.\n  Booked rooms can''t be selected (click is blocked).\n- Adds an availability summary (''3 of 5 available'') and an empty-state\n  message when nothing is available for the dates.\n- If the user''s previously-selected room becomes unavailable when they\n  change dates, the selection is auto-cleared with a toast.\n- Step 3 submit error handler: if the room was booked by someone else\n  between steps, send the user back to Step 1 with a clear message\n  instead of leaving them on the confirm page.\n- RoomCard gains optional ''booked'' + ''bookedReason'' props for the\n  unavailable state.","tree":{"sha":"506189941762696a22d12c0d01277bddc66cf720","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/git/trees/506189941762696a22d12c0d01277bddc66cf720"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/git/commits/f4450de0c12b3f78eccb04161576b7c8f79cc1bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commit/f4450de0c12b3f78eccb04161576b7c8f79cc1bb","node_id":"C_kwDOTTRJJtoAKGY0NDUwZGUwYzEyYjNmNzhlY2NiMDQxNjE1NzZiN2M4Zjc5Y2MxYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commit/852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5","sha":"852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commits/852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5"}],"sha":"f4450de0c12b3f78eccb04161576b7c8f79cc1bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commits/f4450de0c12b3f78eccb04161576b7c8f79cc1bb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commits/852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:49:14Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:49:14Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"e07239bd-96d5-4ae9-bec5-e2536d62482b","tree":{"sha":"fde7d262777a97602a67efd71b4d2c5c30571b60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/git/trees/fde7d262777a97602a67efd71b4d2c5c30571b60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/git/commits/852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commit/852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5","node_id":"C_kwDOTTRJJtoAKDg1MmUwOTQ3YWY3ZGM2NTMxODM5Y2VmMTM5Y2UzNWU3NmFhZDk1YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commit/de6542a2d179fe4dbed8cc6ddc55d32f17b2493d","sha":"de6542a2d179fe4dbed8cc6ddc55d32f17b2493d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carl-YingYang/The_Twenty_Fifth_Web/commits/de6542a2d179fe4dbed8cc6ddc55d32f17b2493d"}],"sha":"852e0947af7dc6531839cef139ce35e76aad95a5